ed in 1067 stands at the water's edge. A considerable portion of the massive town wall (Port Wall ) remains intact as does the Town Gate which provides access from the west. Until the bypass was built a few years ago, access from the east was limited to John Rennie's cast iron 1816 bridge across the river Wye.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Chepstow","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Chepstow","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Chepstow stands where the River Wye meets the Severn in South Wales, an old port town under a Norman castle. Chepstow Castle is the pull, with Tintern Abbey upstream and the Severn Bridge in view, six hours in all between June and September.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":11900,"visit_h":6}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-severn-bridge","name":"Severn Bridge","kind":"Bridge","lat":51.6099,"lon":-2.64026,"dist_km":4.3,"rank_score":9.46,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-chepstow-castle","name":"Chepstow Castle","kind":"Castle","lat":51.6439,"lon":-2.6757,"dist_km":0.3,"rank_score":9.11,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Chepstow_castle_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Chepstow_castle_-_panoramio.jpg","author":"eszgé","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chepstow_castle_-_panoramio.jpg","w":3872,"h":2592,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-tintern-abbey","name":"Tintern Abbey","kind":"Monastery","lat":51.6971,"lon":-2.67722,"dist_km":6.3,"rank_score":7.93,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Tintern_Abbey_and_Courtyard.jpg/960px-Tintern_Abbey_and_Courtyard.jpg","author":"Saffron Blaze","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tintern_Abbey_and_Courtyard.jpg","w":3852,"h":2739,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-prince-of-wales